  <Comment>README

Vocal EQ sane default:
    High-pass: 70–100 Hz
    Cut mud: 200–350 Hz, about 1-4 dB if needed
    Tame boxiness: 500-900 Hz, small cut if needed
    Add presence: 2-5 kHz, small boost if the vocal needs clarity
    Add air: 10-16 kHz, gentle shelf if it needs brightness
Rules of thumb:
    Use wide, subtle moves first.
    If the vocal is harsh, reduce 3-5 kHz before boosting anything.
    If it sounds dull, add a little air instead of pushing presence too hard.</Comment>
